  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
 <para>At a fabric store, fabrics are sold by the yard. A dressmaker spent $36.35 on 4.25 yards of silk and cotton fabrics for a dress. Silk is $16.90 per yard, and cotton is $4 per yard.</para>
 <para>Here is a system of equations that represents the constraints in the situation.</para>
 <para>\(\displaystyle \begin{cases} \begin {align} x + \hspace{2.2mm} y &amp;=
   \hspace{2mm} 4.25\\ 16.90x + 4y &amp;= 36.35 \end{align} \end{cases} \)</para>
 
 <!--Q1-->
 <exercise>
   <problem>
     <para>
         What does the solution to the system represent?
       </para>
     </problem><solution>
     
     <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
   <para>Compare your answer:</para>
     <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. The solution represents the combination of lengths of silk and cotton (in yards) that meet both constraints: they add up to 4.25 yards, and the cost of buying both is $36.35.</para>
   </solution></exercise>
 <!--Interaction End -->
 
 <!--Q2-->
 <exercise>
   <problem>
     <para>
         Find the solution to the system of equations. 
       </para>
     </problem><solution>
     
     <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
   <para>Compare your answer:</para>
     <para>1.5 yards of silk and 2.75 yards of cotton.</para>
   </solution></exercise>
 <!--Interaction End -->
 
 <!--Q3-->
 <exercise>
   <problem>
     <para>
         Explain or show how you know.
       </para>
     </problem><solution>
     
     <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
   <para>Compare your answer:</para>
     <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
     <list>
       <item>
         The graphs of the equations intersect at
       
       \((1.5,2.75)\)
         
         <figure><media alt="Graph of a linear system. cotton (yards), silk (yards)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/00b4ac90c051ada23ff5235d9161f8ff72d6c048"/></media></figure></item>
       <item> Solving by using a table gives \(x=1.5\) and \(y=2.75\).</item>
     </list>
   </solution></exercise>
 <!--Interaction End --></section>
